    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0836" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/807</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Langhorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-19T17:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 19, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>487. For Department of Commerce.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>87. Await your answer my 86. Have reliable information to the effect that
                        might obtain 800 tons colors if I can go to Berlin next Monday with a <pb
                            facs="0837" n="551" xml:id="pg551"/> guarantee that British Navy will
                        not interfere. Important that you should answer at once. What are the
                        prospects? <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thompson</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Commercial Attaché</hi>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langhorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
